Set an application password to a caller-supplied value.

kanidm mints application passwords itself and returns the cleartext exactly once
(server/lib/src/idm/application.rs, readable_password_from_random). That is right
for what the feature was designed for -- a person asking for a password to paste
into a mail client on their phone -- and wrong for declarative provisioning,
where the secret is generated offline into a secret store and the server may not
be running at the time it is created.

This adds a SECOND path rather than changing the first. `secret` on
ScimApplicationPasswordCreate is optional and defaults to None, which is what
every existing client sends, so generate-and-return is untouched and a person
still cannot choose their own application password.

What the provisioning path keeps:

  * ADMINISTRATOR ONLY. Supplying a secret is refused unless the caller is a
    member of idm_admins. The event carries the CALLER's identity rather than an
    internal one, so access controls still apply underneath -- the membership
    check narrows the API surface, it is not the only thing enforcing this.
  * NO CREDENTIAL REUSE. The secret is rejected if it already authenticates for
    another application, or for this one under another label. That is the
    property the feature exists for -- one credential must not span applications
    -- and it is enforced in the server rather than trusted to the provisioner.
  * IDEMPOTENT. A provisioning tool runs on every start, and Password::new
    salts, so writing unconditionally would store a different value every boot.
    When the password already verifies for this application and label, nothing
    is modified and the existing uuid is returned.

Checked against v1.11.2 before building, since kanidmd_lib is #![deny(warnings)]
and the build is measured in hours:

  * applies cleanly (patch --dry-run against the files at tag v1.11.2)
  * Modify, ModifyList, Value, PartialValue, Attribute and UUID_IDM_ADMINS all
    come from the preludes these files already import
  * ModifyList::new_list(Vec<Modify>) exists (server/lib/src/modify.rs:103)
  * internal_search_uuid is on QueryServerTransaction, already used in this file
  * Identity::is_memberof exists (server/lib/src/server/identity.rs:362)
  * OperationError::{NotAuthorised, InvalidRequestState} both exist
  * Account::try_from_entry_rw and ApplicationPassword's application/label/
    password fields are pub(crate), and the caller is in the same crate
  * every struct-literal construction of ScimApplicationPasswordCreate is
    updated. #[serde(default)] covers the wire format but NOT a literal, so the
    cli and testkit sites are compile errors without this -- four of them,
    found by searching rather than by waiting for the build

